---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Supported Contests – ContestLogX">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center px-5 py-10">

    <div class="max-w-4xl w-full">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">Supported Contests</h1>

      <p class="text-lg opacity-80 mb-12">
        ContestLogX supports a wide variety of amateur radio contests through user-defined JSON modules.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg border p-8" style="background-color: #161b22; border-color: #30363d;">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Built-in Contest Modules</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 mb-12">
          <li>ARRL 10 Meter Contest</li>
          <li>ARRL VHF Contest</li>
          <li>CWops Tests (CWT)</li>
          <li>North American QSO Party (NAQP)</li>
          <li>Winter Field Day</li>
          <li>YBDX</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Custom Contest Support</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          ContestLogX allows you to define your own contest modules using a simple JSON format.
          This means you can create support for any contest, customizing exchange fields,
          scoring rules, multipliers, and more.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
